+    # §8 primal-ray extraction (CORRECTED per advisor review 2026-07-28).
+    # This is a Max-λ / homogeneous-equality SOS conic problem. When Mosek
+    # reports primal_status = INFEASIBILITY_CERTIFICATE it has found an unbounded
+    # improving ray of the *primal* model; the ray lives in the VARIABLE VALUES
+    # value.(pos/gpos/λ), NOT in dual(con_eq) (the earlier dual() attempt read
+    # the wrong side and returned degenerate zeros). A valid infeasibility/
+    # dual-infeasibility certificate requires ALL of:
+    #   (a) λ_ray > 0                (genuine improving direction)
+    #   (b) every pos[i] ⪰ 0          (ray stays in the positivity cone)
+    #   (c) every gpos[l] ⪰ 0         (ray stays in the gap cone)
+    #   (d) cons residual ≈ 0         (the homogeneous affine identity holds)
+    # (d) is evaluated by JuMP's value.(cons), independent of the solver flag.
+    # NOTE: under SLOW_PROGRESS the ray is a candidate only; (a)-(d) must pass
+    # and ideally be re-checked with rational/interval post-processing.
+    cert_ray = nothing
+    cert_artifact = nothing
